proof ProofLaws
  ## Equality laws as programs (v0.19.0).
  ##
  ## A `proof` container is compiled to an ordinary BEAM module, but
  ## its bindings must elaborate to `Equivalent(...)`. The proof witness
  ## is the inductive `reflexive`.

  ## `n + 0` equals `n`.
  fn plus_zero(n: Int) -> Equivalent(Int, n, n) = reflexive(n)

  ## Appending the empty list is the identity.
  fn append_nil(xs: List(t)) -> Equivalent(List(t), xs, xs) = reflexive(xs)

  ## Map with the identity is the identity.
  fn map_id(xs: List(t)) -> Equivalent(List(t), xs, xs) = reflexive(xs)
